{"id":"l3","level":6,"levelName":"Reading literature","n":5,"of":11,"title":"Directions and other survivals","titleHe":"ה׳ הַמְּגַמָּה","goal":"Read the ־ָה that means towards, and the other fossils around it.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"An unstressed ־ָה on the end of a place noun means towards it — a case ending that survived nowhere else."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הַבַּיְתָה","en":"homewards, home"},{"he":"אַרְצָה","en":"to the land, to Israel"},{"he":"יְרוּשָׁלַיְמָה","en":"to Jerusalem"},{"he":"הַחוּצָה","en":"outwards, outside"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"הַבַּיְתָה is fully alive in modern Hebrew — אֲנִי הוֹלֵךְ הַבַּיְתָה, I'm going home. Most of the others are literary."},{"type":"text","body":"Two more worth knowing: the infinitive with לְ can appear as בְּ or כְּ plus the infinitive to mean when — בְּבוֹאוֹ, when he came — and the particle אֵת is often spelled אֶת־ with a hyphen in older typesetting."}],"vocab":[{"he":"הַבַּיְתָה","en":"homewards","translit":"habayta"},{"he":"אַרְצָה","en":"to the land","translit":"artsa"},{"he":"הַחוּצָה","en":"outside","translit":"hachutsa"},{"he":"שָׁמַיִם","en":"sky, heaven","translit":"shamayim"},{"he":"לֵאמֹר","en":"saying (introduces speech)","translit":"lemor"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["coming of age at thirteen","the blessing over wine","full","homewards"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הַבַּיְתָה","translit":"habayta"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in the end","sees","good","to the land"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אַרְצָה","translit":"artsa"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sleeps","my, mine","outside","it is permitted"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הַחוּצָה","translit":"hachutsa"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["with him","manager","thousand","sky, heaven"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שָׁמַיִם","translit":"shamayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["land, country","believes","saying (introduces speech)","helped (someone)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לֵאמֹר","translit":"lemor"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["הַבַּיְתָה","homewards"],["אַרְצָה","to the land"],["הַחוּצָה","outside"],["שָׁמַיִם","sky, heaven"],["לֵאמֹר","saying (introduces speech)"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sky, heaven”?","options":["עַל יְדֵי","שָׁמַיִם","בִּכְלָל","קוֹנֶה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["שָׁמַיִם","הַחוּצָה","הַבַּיְתָה","אַרְצָה"],"correct":1,"say":"הַחוּצָה","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “to the land”?","options":["סְפֵק","שָׁקֵט","כָּזֶה","אַרְצָה"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “saying (introduces speech)”?","options":["חַלָּשׁ","לֵאמֹר","כִּסֵּא","כָּאן"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"לֵאמֹר","translit":"lemor","en":"saying (introduces speech)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “homewards”?","options":["מְקַבֵּל","כָּתֹם","הַבַּיְתָה","וַיְהִי"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “sky, heaven” in Hebrew","answer":"שָׁמַיִם","hint":"shamayim"}]}